sequenceDiagram
    autonumber

    box rgb(239, 246, 255) Runtime router
      participant USER as User question
      participant API as FastAPI chat API
      participant ST1 as Stage1 request type
      participant ST2 as Stage2 agent route
      participant GATE as Runtime gate
    end

    box rgb(238, 242, 255) Service agents
      participant AGENT as Selected service agent
      participant LG as LangGraph orchestration
    end

    box rgb(245, 243, 255) PostgreSQL schemas and knowledge sources
      participant ONT as OntologyContext
      participant DOCKB as OpsEnergyDoc
      participant OPSDB as OpsWorkOrder
      participant MART as MartFacts
      participant REF as ReferenceSchemaTimeSeries
      participant OPSREPORT as OpsReportSchema
    end

    box rgb(236, 253, 245) Backend outputs
      participant ANSWER as Chat response
      participant STATUS as Job status response
      participant APPROVAL as Approval state
    end

    box rgb(240, 249, 255) Frontend UI
      participant FRONT as React dashboard UI
    end

    USER->>API: submit /api/chat question
    API->>ST1: classify request type
    alt query request
      ST1->>ST2: classify agent route
      ST2->>AGENT: dispatch to anomaly, cms, report, forecast, or domain_qa
      AGENT->>ONT: lookup meter and measurement context
      AGENT->>DOCKB: lookup document KB when needed
      AGENT->>REF: lookup reference time-series facts
      AGENT->>MART: lookup mart facts when needed
      AGENT->>OPSREPORT: lookup report tables when needed
      AGENT-->>ANSWER: build answer with route metadata
      ANSWER-->>API: return /api/chat result
      API-->>FRONT: render chat output and caveats
    else action, approval, off_topic, or multi_intent
      ST1->>GATE: enter clarify, reject, or approval wait gate
      GATE->>LG: create review state only when runtime action needs review
      LG->>OPSDB: read or prepare work order state
      LG->>ONT: attach domain context
      LG->>REF: attach supporting numeric facts
      LG-->>STATUS: expose job status and caveats
      LG-->>APPROVAL: wait for human approval when required
      STATUS-->>API: return status path and progress payload
      APPROVAL-->>API: return pending approval state
      API-->>FRONT: render status, caveat, or approval UI
    end

    Note over ST1,ST2: Stage1 handles request policy. Stage2 runs only for query requests.
    Note over LG,OPSDB: LangGraph coordinates guarded review state and never performs canonical promotion directly.
    Note over ONT,REF: Runtime grounding uses ops, mart, reference, ontology and ops.energy_doc sources.
